in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @peer
in @aikido
in @aikido/reflect
in @time

# @peer/reflect — Tier-1 peer response species; the operational
# dispatcher to @aikido/reflect at peer altitude.
#
# Species under @peer (sibling to @peer/void `9c7de83`, @peer/persistence,
# @peer/registry, @peer/beam). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara Round-3 per
# Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.7.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Tier 1 of the three-tier @peer response surface (per
# `shards/aikido.mirror` §The three-tier response surface):
#
#   Tier 1 (default; this species) — @peer.reflect dispatches
#     @aikido/reflect.aikido_reflect_of_surface_class per algedonic-
#     below-Tier-1 discipline.
#   Tier 2 (escalation) — @peer.redirect walks Crystal chain backwards.
#     Sibling shard: `shards/peer/redirect.mirror` (this tick).
#   Tier 3 (recognition bomb) — @peer.reframe dispatches @cyberpunk/
#     bugz with lens payload. Sibling shard: `shards/peer/reframe.
#     mirror` (this tick).
#
# @peer/reflect is the DEFAULT: when a peer is asked a question and
# no algedonic threshold has fired, @peer.reflect is the response.
# The peer sees the question, reflects the substrate-honest reading
# back, and holds no demand for the frame's acceptance.
#
# === Composition-primitive naming ===
#
# Per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention:
#
#   peer_reflect_of_perturbation(p: peer, perturbation: ref)
#     -> question
#
# Input-shape: `perturbation` (the incoming perturbation the peer is
# metabolizing). Output: `question` (the reflected witnessed answer
# surfacing as a question to the operator's frame).
#
# === Dispatch discipline ===
#
# `peer_reflect_of_perturbation` constructs an @aikido/reflect
# aikido_context from (p, perturbation, current-timestamp, peer's
# viable_system, peer's algedonic-reading) and dispatches to
# `@aikido/reflect.aikido_reflect_of_surface_class(reflect, ctx)`.
# The composition:
#
#   1. Sample peer's own @cyberpunk/algedonic reading of perturbation
#      severity.
#   2. Classify surface_class per algedonic threshold (Tier-1 iff
#      below Tier-1 boundary; per §Escalation is peer-internal in
#      @aikido.mirror).
#   3. Construct aikido_context (perturbation, surface_class,
#      algedonic_reading, viable_system, timestamp).
#   4. Dispatch @aikido/reflect.aikido_reflect_of_surface_class.
#   5. Return the resulting question (per @mirror/reflection three-
#      operation discharge).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/peer/reflect.mirror`** — clean naming space.
# 2. **`shards/peer/void.mirror`** (`9c7de83`) — reviewed. Sibling
#    species under @peer at K=0 duality-basis altitude. Distinct
#    altitude from @peer/reflect (Tier-1 aikido dispatcher); no
#    conflict.
# 3. **`shards/peer.mirror`** — reviewed. Family-root with .load and
#    .audhd actions; @peer/reflect adds Tier-1 dispatcher as sibling
#    species, does not modify family-root surface.
# 4. **`shards/mirror/reflection.mirror`** — reviewed. Sibling species-
#    under-@mirror at 3-operation reflection discipline. @peer/reflect
#    ROUTES through @aikido/reflect which DISPATCHES @mirror/
#    reflection; three altitudes; no conflict.
#
# === The peer_reflect_response carrier ===
#
# The typed return of `peer_reflect_of_perturbation`. Composes:
#
#   question       — the reflected witnessed answer per @mirror/
#                     reflection dispatch.
#   aikido_context — the constructed context (for the peer's own
#                     trajectory record).
#   discharge_verdict — the verdict of the aikido_reflect_of_surface_
#                     class dispatch.
type peer_reflect_response = {
  question:          ref,
  aikido_context:    ref,
  discharge_verdict: verdict,
}

# === peer_reflect_of_perturbation — the Tier-1 dispatcher action ===
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `peer=reflect-tier-1-dispatch-to-
# aikido-reflect`.
peer_reflect_of_perturbation(p: peer, perturbation: ref)
  -> peer_reflect_response
requires peer_reflect_admissible(p, perturbation)
{ \ }

# === peer_reflect_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - p is a well-formed peer (per @peer.load discipline)
#   - perturbation is byte-visible (Rice-safe)
#   - the peer's own @cyberpunk/algedonic reading of perturbation
#     falls BELOW the peer's Tier-1 threshold (per @cyberpunk/
#     algedonic discipline; the substrate-decl'd boundary at which
#     Tier-1 fires vs Tier-2)
#   - the peer's viable_system carrier discharges viable_well_formed
#
# Sentinel: `peer=reflect-tier-1-admissible-below-algedonic-threshold`.
bilateral peer_reflect_admissible {
  sentinel "peer=reflect-tier-1-admissible-below-algedonic-threshold"
  arity 2
}
peer_reflect_admissible(p: peer, perturbation: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Recognition candidates surfaced (DO NOT RATIFY at this landing)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# #R-peer-reflect-is-the-substrate-native-default-response — Tier-1
# is the default; a peer at rest returns witnessed questions, not
# affirmations. First-witness this tick. Second-witness gate opens
# on Reed's post-Round-3 pillar firing. Held at CANDIDATE strength.
#
# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - peer_reflect_witnessing bilateral composing peer_reflect_
#   admissible + aikido_reflect_of_surface_class discharge
# - .reflect cli-boundary wrapper at @mirror/peer altitude

out @peer/reflect
out peer_reflect_response
out peer_reflect_of_perturbation
out peer_reflect_admissible
